cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Seldon: Out-of-Sample Forecasting of Armed Conflicts, Currency Crises, and Banking Crises"
message: "If you use Seldon's code, evaluation benchmarks, or frozen forecast vintages in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Angelina
    family-names: Volina
repository-code: "https://github.com/unicat-42/seldon"
url: "https://github.com/unicat-42/seldon"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
abstract: >-
  Point-in-time, strictly out-of-sample probabilistic early-warning models for state-based armed
  conflict onset, currency devaluations, and systemic banking crises across 174 countries, with a
  regional lens on the 15 post-Soviet states, automated look-ahead leakage tests, publication-lag
  enforcement, and immutable monthly forecast vintages.
keywords:
  - armed conflict prediction
  - conflict forecasting
  - currency crisis
  - banking crisis
  - financial crisis prediction
  - early warning system
  - geopolitical risk
  - country risk
  - point-in-time backtesting
  - out-of-sample forecasting
  - publication lags
  - exchange market pressure
  - post-Soviet economies
  - UCDP
  - PITF
